{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383456-mta-2e-interesting-use-of-spheres","id":1383456,"title":"MtA 2E - Interesting Use of Spheres","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-23T15:34:34-07:00","id":1383456,"title":"MtA 2E - Interesting Use of Spheres","content":"I am joining a game soon with my new mage character. I chose the spheres Correspondence 3, Mind 3, Prime 2. I have Arete 5 so I should have an ok time casting most spells. I am trying to come up with cool, fun, or interesting combinations for these but can't think of a lot past scanning buildings, teleportation, sensing my surroundings. Any ideas would be greatly appreciated!<br /> <br /> Edit: The mage I am making will be shooting guns and currently has 3 in firearms and 4 in dexterity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24181,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","user":"Donavan","date":". 04-23-2020, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","name":"Donavan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T16:11:10-07:00","id":1383465,"title":"","content":"I have a player in my games who has nearly that exact same sphere loadout!<br /> <br /> I'll be a little general with the ideas, but...<br /> <br /> 1) Mind 3 Prime 2 to summon up semi real illusions that do mind pattern damage aggravated. Imagine summoning up an quasi-real rocket launcher that does emotional damage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2) Infrasound / Vibes at a distance, basically Correspondence 2 / Mind 2 / Prime 2 to conjure up a massive amount of bad or good vibes in a distant location to suffuse the place in some shady resonance or demoralise your opponents.<br /> <br /> 3) Calm Under Pressure, a conjunctional Correspondence 1 and Mind 1 effect to not only set your firearms difficulty at Point Blank but to also reduce or even nullify increased difficulty from auto fire for a scenne<br /> <br /> 4) This is a little fringe, but a Correspondence 3 Mind 3 ban to ban emotions or Resonances from a location","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T17:47:14-07:00","id":1383480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383456-mta-2e-interesting-use-of-spheres?p=1383465#post1383465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) This is a little fringe, but a Correspondence 3 Mind 3 ban to ban emotions or Resonances from a location</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a place where people can't get angry or sad?<br /> <br /> Anti hostility ward! Actively hostile people (people currently looking to actively hurt or destroy something) can't pass.<br /> <br /> @Donovan You should Probably find a way to use Mind 3 and Correspondence 3 to ban mind reading and control, as I think the ban is much tougher than your usual mind shielding. Maybe also make a ward against some levels of unwanted magic with Correspondence 3 Mind 3 Prime 2 while you are at it? Depending on what your storyteller will allow.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing you could use Mind 3 to hide the fact that you are carrying many many guns. Maybe even Mind 3 Correspondence 2 to make some sort of ranged illusion that affects even people using cameras from the other side of the world so long as they are aware of you and have that form of illusionary closeness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T18:21:12-07:00","id":1383487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383456-mta-2e-interesting-use-of-spheres?p=1383465#post1383465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2) Infrasound / Vibes at a distance, basically Correspondence 2 / Mind 2 / Prime 2 to conjure up a massive amount of bad or good vibes in a distant location to suffuse the place in some shady resonance or demoralise your opponents.<br /> <br /> 3) Calm Under Pressure, a conjunctional Correspondence 1 and Mind 1 effect to not only set your firearms difficulty at Point Blank but to also reduce or even nullify increased difficulty from auto fire for a scenne</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like these two I'm writing them down <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383456-mta-2e-interesting-use-of-spheres?p=1383480#post1383480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> @Donovan You should Probably find a way to use Mind 3 and Correspondence 3 to ban mind reading and control, as I think the ban is much tougher than your usual mind shielding. Maybe also make a ward against some levels of unwanted magic with Correspondence 3 Mind 3 Prime 2 while you are at it? Depending on what your storyteller will allow.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing you could use Mind 3 to hide the fact that you are carrying many many guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya I hadn't really planned to much for anti magic. We are all mages in the group and he did say the game would involve mage warfare. As for the guns yes I have many many guns. He allowed us to take backgrounds from other books if they made sense and I ended up taking armory 3 and resources 3. I'll have just about any weapon you could want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","name":"Donavan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T02:54:37-07:00","id":1383545,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12480_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12480\" data-vbnamecard=\"12480\">Spacecat</a> I really like the anti hostility ward idea, sort of like how the Elysium mechanic worked in Vtmb<br /> <br /> Also, a rote one of my player's is figuring out is a sort of adaptation of Mind 3, Prime 2 and Correspondence 3 where you create a really emotionally draining area that can functionally set your Permanent Willpower score to a lower score (temporarily ofc) the longer you're there, which might interfere with your Arete use. A little strong and something you'd want to speak with your ST about, but it can be very useful if you're trying to trap rooms or locations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T04:26:56-07:00","id":1383558,"title":"","content":"@Distant : Choir. How about Mind 3 Prime 2 for a Willpower point destroying mind blast? Though you're probably better off with a machine gun.<br /> <br /> @Donovan : How about a tank with an illusion that makes it seem like a car?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T04:27:54-07:00","id":1383559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383456-mta-2e-interesting-use-of-spheres?p=1383465#post1383465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Mind 3 Prime 2 to summon up semi real illusions that do mind pattern damage aggravated. Imagine summoning up an quasi-real rocket launcher that does emotional damage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This made me laugh out loud. Ready the CareBear familiars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:34:45-07:00","id":1383575,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> Never underestimate the power of friendship rockets.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12480_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12480\" data-vbnamecard=\"12480\">Spacecat</a> I suppose in some ways it's a little more subtle and coincidental; if you're using speakers to give someone a scathing critique from a distance it would make sense to flay their willpower points?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T08:00:48-07:00","id":1383602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You should Probably find a way to use Mind 3 and Correspondence 3 to ban mind reading and control, as I think the ban is much tougher than your usual mind shielding</div> </div> </div> </div>Pilling on this:<br /> <br /> Mind 1 it's enough to shield/ban, but because Mind it's the Sphere of illusions, at higher levels you can control what the spy sees instead of merely causing the attempt to fail. An example would be the Mind 2 No Mind of the Akashicks that makes potential mental spies detect no toughts at all instead of knowingly fail. I would say that at 3 you could do things like craft fake tougths and memories to be read.<br /> <br /> Corr 2 bans scrying (may be essential in magely warfare). Arguably with Mind 3 you could make failed would be scriers see an illusion instead - which not only controls the flow of information, but also discourages trying again with more successes.<br /> <br /> With Corr 3/Mind 3, I think you could <i>arguably</i> be able to cause damage to anyone that tries to control your mind, as per the more aggresive wards of HDYDT (Aggravated with Prime 2, ouch! not very nice, but then, neither it's mind control). <hr />For guns Corr allows amazing shoots. You can potentially teleport a shoot anywhere in the world you have a connection with, but that's likely going Vulgar. Less Vulgar would be to make the bullets change trajectory, which Corr can also do. Eventually you may want to get Forces if you want to go for the gun toothing Mage.<br /> <br /> OP already said scanning, still it bears repeating: Knowing where the targets are it's very good for sniping, to ambush enemies, and to counter potential snipers and other ambushes. And about ambushes, Mind being the sphere of illusions, at 3 it arguably should be able to hide your pressence from the minds of others.<br /> <br /> It may be relevant to mention that the spells you will cast and how you will cast them it's largely informed by your Focus (and general approach to magick). If you tell us what's your Focus, that could be a source of more thematical ideas for your character","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-24-2020, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T08:49:35-07:00","id":1383608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383456-mta-2e-interesting-use-of-spheres?p=1383602#post1383602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may be relevant to mention that the spells you will cast and how you will cast them it's largely informed by your Focus (and general approach to magick). If you tell us what's your Focus, that could be a source of more thematical ideas for your character</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks I enjoyed these ideas.<br /> <br /> As for the focus what I had come to was runes/symbols(They are all over his house, vehicle, guns, bullets, usually in hidden areas), meditation(Mostly for the mind stuff but applies to everything I.E. taking a deep breath to center yourself as you take the shot), and verbal components(without trying to sound cheesy something like D&amp;D magic where some spells have spoken components).<br /> <br /> His awakening was very traumatic. A group of sabbat came through his apartment complex and drained him, and most of the building, nearly dry then threw him off a roof. His powers awakened at that point and the correspondence kicked in to soften the blow from hitting the ground(didn't fall as far). A band of hunters came through and found him. Seeing there was something different they assumed he was a newly awakened hunter so they brought him back to their camp and he trained with them for awhile until they figured out he was a mage and tried to kill him. At that point he left and has been on his own still hunting using his mage powers to augment his abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","name":"Donavan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T09:19:31-07:00","id":1383612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Donavan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383456-mta-2e-interesting-use-of-spheres?p=1383608#post1383608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the focus what I had come to was runes/symbols(They are all over his house, vehicle, guns, bullets, usually in hidden areas), meditation(Mostly for the mind stuff but applies to everything I.E. taking a deep breath to center yourself as you take the shot), and verbal components(without trying to sound cheesy something like D&amp;D magic where some spells have spoken components).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm sorry. I meant his Paradigm. Didn't look at the 2e clarification, M20 calls the Paradigm Focus. Still, knowing your focuses it's also important to guess these things. I do think all effects mentioned are very appropiate, easy to imagine wards, charms and mind shields with runes and meditation, and it's also very D&amp;D-esque to cast illusions of all kinds.<br /> <br /> It's your character from some Tradition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-24-2020, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T09:30:49-07:00","id":1383615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383456-mta-2e-interesting-use-of-spheres?p=1383612#post1383612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I'm sorry. I meant his Paradigm. Didn't look at the 2e clarification, M20 calls the Paradigm Focus. Still, knowing your focuses it's also important to guess these things. I do think all effects mentioned are very appropiate, easy to imagine wards, charms and mind shields with runes and meditation, and it's also very D&amp;D-esque to cast illusions of all kinds.<br /> <br /> It's your character from some Tradition?</div> </div> </div> </div>He hasn't really had any contact with other mages up until right when we start our game. At this point he is classified as an Orphan I believe. Much of what he knows is self taught. I had though of things like the scope of my rifle has runes etched into the glass. Makes it pretty much unusuable for a normal person since you can't see into the scope now but for Correspondance spells it is a semi-foci. As for the paradigm thats something I never really understood. Like I figured out how my character casts spells with the things I mentioned above but as for his view of everything....i'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","name":"Donavan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T12:55:41-07:00","id":1383662,"title":"","content":"Small update. I stumbled across the Sanctum background and talked to my ST. He said I could use that so I will be putting a few points into it. With the reduced difficulty for casting rituals I would be able to do a lot more from relative safety of my sanctum.<br /> <br /> Edit: If I saved up exp and went to Correspondence 4 it lets me co-locate myself. If I used C4/M3/P2 would I be able to co-locate myself but without a physical body there but that would still be able to do damage? I could sit in my sanctuary meditating projecting myself out into the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24181,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","user":"Donavan","date":". 04-24-2020, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","name":"Donavan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T20:06:03-07:00","id":1383900,"title":"","content":"I'm not entirely sure how you'd co-locate without a body as co-location tends to mean you are in both spots. I guess your storyteller will have to figure that out. <br /> <br /> As an alternative, with Mind 3 and Correspondence 3 (or 2 depending on the Storyteller) you could probably already project your awareness and a seemingly real illusion of yourself. Then you can use Prime 3 (and mind 3) to turn the illusion into an aggravated damage dealing Kung Fu machine<br /> <br /> Edit: not sure how you'd hold stuff and operate doors without Forces but you can look like you do since you are a mental illusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-25-2020, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T19:54:20-07:00","id":1384080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383456-mta-2e-interesting-use-of-spheres?p=1383900#post1383900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not entirely sure how you'd co-locate without a body as co-location tends to mean you are in both spots. I guess your storyteller will have to figure that out.<br /> <br /> As an alternative, with Mind 3 and Correspondence 3 (or 2 depending on the Storyteller) you could probably already project your awareness and a seemingly real illusion of yourself. Then you can use Prime 3 (and mind 3) to turn the illusion into an aggravated damage dealing Kung Fu machine<br /> <br /> Edit: not sure how you'd hold stuff and operate doors without Forces but you can look like you do since you are a mental illusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in answer to this. My ST did say co-locating would be Corr 4. It says that in the book. What I did was use the co-located senses(correspondance 3) with mind 3 to project an illusion of myself into that area. I then just put my senses on top of that illusion. I used prime 2 to weave a small amount of pattern into my illusion to make it 'semi real'. Its not really there but the only thing I did with it was knock on a door, speak, and pat someone on the cheek to assure them I was real. It worked great. I stayed in my Sactun the entire time and as my group called it &quot;Lokied around&quot;. The way my ST described it was anytime someone looked at me with sensing magic I was there but not there. When a mage xrayed my he saw my body but couldn't really see any bones. When he looked at me with force my energy was there but not really like it should be. He was pretty persistent but I just kept pushing back to our plan at hand and he eventually conceded and ignored it. I accidentally gave it away when I said I had a book about what we were discussing and I accidentally walked through a wall in that area to get a book in my sanctum.<br /> <br /> After actually getting into the game I fell right into uses for them. One of my favorites was at the end of the story we had finished dealing with the government who was trying to hunt down and capture mages. I was going to teleport everyone back and I used Mind 3/Correspondance 3 to teleport everyone back to their homes into their beds. They all woke up the next morning wondering if any of it actually happened. I have Arcane5 and my ST immediately picked up I was playing into it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It was a great game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","name":"Donavan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T19:58:26-07:00","id":1384082,"title":"","content":"Oh one other really cool thing. I used mind 3 to link our group together to do magic in tandem. That way when I used correspondance everyone else in the link would get the senes the sames thing I did. When our healing mage used life magic to detect people all of us would detect them. Ect. We used this in concert with a mage who had force 4 to cause an earthquake that did almost no damage to the civilian population but destroyed a secret underground government facility. In the end after a multi hour ritual that involved 4 mages who all had 4+ arete we destroyed the base with a combined sphere use of Force4/Correspondance3/Mind3/Life2/Prime2. On the down side our ST has told us out of character the technocracy has 100% taken notice of this and the government will be looking to find ways to not let this happen again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","name":"Donavan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T20:35:39-07:00","id":1384091,"title":"","content":"Awesome. Great game. <br /> <br /> With regards to Correspondence 4 co-location, I just mean that if you really co-locate to two places, you could usually get shot in both locations and not all Storytellers will allow partial co-locations of just your presence while you are safe at home.<br /> <br /> I once had this idea of using co-location and then boosting my mind so that I could multitask really really well, and properly hold a steady job while, crafting a magical item, while researching the supernatural, while adventuring with my peers. <br /> <br /> I hope for you to have more awesome games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T20:44:39-07:00","id":1384092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the down side our ST has told us out of character the technocracy has 100% taken notice of this and the government will be looking to find ways to not let this happen again. </div> </div> </div>Notorious already. Awesome. Now is the time to build multiple bolt holes, and maybe an army or superweapon! Assuming that's the type of game you are playing, of course. Also, you might want to figure out what your final victory condition for your war will be (like create a Tradition territory that the Tech won't dare step into, force peace talks, get rid of every Tech installation in the world and shunt the rest into the deep Umbra...) Note that if you get too dangerous to the tech, you might become a candidate for nuking or orbital bombardment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T06:11:32-07:00","id":1384174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1383456-mta-2e-interesting-use-of-spheres?p=1384092#post1384092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Notorious already. Awesome. Now is the time to build multiple bolt holes, and maybe an army or superweapon! Assuming that's the type of game you are playing, of course. Also, you might want to figure out what your final victory condition for your war will be (like create a Tradition territory that the Tech won't dare step into, force peace talks, get rid of every Tech installation in the world and shunt the rest into the deep Umbra...) Note that if you get too dangerous to the tech, you might become a candidate for nuking or orbital bombardment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We have no idea what kind of game we are playing lol. I've played in a WoD campaign once before and for the rest of the group its their first time. The ST has run numerous campaigns for WoD. He said he had to spend his week figuring out how all the NPCs in the world react to what has just happened.<br /> <br /> As for the orbital bomb, our mage that has time looked forward to see possible outcomes and we were told one is a future in which the city we live in just doesn't exist. A paradox bomb goes off at its center and it is removed from the timeline all together.<br /> <br /> I was actually really surprised. I tend to be a bit of a rollplayer and I love combat in DnD. We technically didn't have a single combat role in almost five hours. Just a good amount of RP of our characters getting introduced and being given a problem. It was fantastic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24181,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","user":"Donavan","date":". 04-27-2020, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","name":"Donavan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T06:44:25-07:00","id":1384180,"title":"","content":"I guess making a paradox bomb should be scratched off the list of possible superweapons... I so wish I could play Mage with you folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T10:26:25-07:00","id":1386110,"title":"","content":"I had an idea suddenly and wanted to know if this would work how I think it would. Correspondence 3 allows you to collocate senses but without Mind X you can't make sense of it. Would it be possible to force Correspondence 3 onto someone else making them fully aware of everything happening around them all at the same time but without using the Mind sphere and overload their senses?<br /> <br /> Sadly we did not get to game this last so I've had to much time to think <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: Or use the Mind sphere to make it harder to understand and overload the mind easier?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24181,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","user":"Donavan","date":". 05-06-2020, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","name":"Donavan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T10:33:28-07:00","id":1386114,"title":"","content":"You need Mind 2 to share senses and as they will likely be unwilling recipients of your heightened senses you will need to score a number of success equal to their Willpower. If they are supernatural they will have the chance to defend with their Willpower with an opposed roll.<br /> <br /> I absolutely love this and think this idea is hilarious. What a way to screw with people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T07:27:11-07:00","id":1386685,"title":"","content":"I have been using Mind3/Correspondance3 to make illusion copies of myself out in the world outside of my house and putting my senses on top of it. Mind 3 was used to help mask the illusion better. Giving all the normal senses I would give if I was real. So I touch someone and they &quot;feel&quot; me even though they don't really. If I added Life2 and/or Prime2 to that would it allow a semi real copy of me? One that I could still dismiss when I wanted to but would be physically there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","name":"Donavan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T17:32:25-07:00","id":1386832,"title":"","content":"I don't think Life 2 would be enough to create a &quot;real&quot; physical copy of yourself, though perhaps Prime 2 would be enough to make the illusion solid and thus pass for same to casual inspection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}